<h3 id=3D"model-development">Model Development</h3>
<h4 id=3D"model-selection">Model selection</h4>
<p>We choose neural networks because:</p>
<ul>
<li>Neural networks are good at handling unstructured data, such as images =
and text</li>
<li>Unlike many traditional machine learning models, neural networks are ab=
le to produce the embeddings we need for representation learning</li>
</ul>
<p>What types of neural network architectures should we use? It is essentia=
l that the architecture works with images. CNN-based architectures such as =
ResNet [4] or more recent Transformer-based architectures [5] such as ViT [=
6] perform well with image inputs. Figure 2.5 shows a simplified model arch=
itecture that transforms the input image into an embedding vector. The numb=
er of convolution layers, the number of neurons in fullyconnected layers, a=
nd the size of the embedding vector are hyperparameters typically chosen vi=
a experimentation.</p>
