<p>A high CTR indicates that users click on the displayed items often. CTR =
is commonly used as an online metric in search and recommendation systems, =
as we will see in later chapters.</p>
<p><strong>Average daily, weekly, and monthly time spent on the suggested i=
mages.</strong> This metric shows how engaged users are with the suggested =
images. When the search system is accurate, we expect this metric to increa=
se.</p>
<h3 id=3D"serving">Serving</h3>
<p>At serving time, the system returns a ranked list of similar images base=
d on a query image. Figure 2.19 shows the prediction pipeline and an indexi=
